// hs op unattended (nginx=auto): nginx from nginx.org's own repository.
// Hestia installs nginx from nginx.org (mainline), so Debian's security
// updates never reach it. On 2026-10-21 six of nine boxes still ran a version
// open to CVE-2026-42533 (RCE, public exploit since July; fixed in 1.31.3).
// The package upgrade tests the config first, then swaps the binary in place
// (USR2): no connection drops. If the test fails the old binary keeps running;
// hs check (updates.nginx-binary) reports that.
// The panel's own nginx (hestia-nginx) comes from apt.hestiacp.com, not here.
Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern {
        "origin=nginx,label=nginx";
};
